@hyperframes/core 0.8.209: package.json has no license field; LICENSE is the Apache-2.0 text.
@hyperframes/engine 0.8.209: package.json has no license field; LICENSE is the Apache-2.0 text. Modified by Taalcut (patches/@hyperframes__engine@0.8.209.patch): dist/utils/managedChildProcess.js, dist/utils/gpuEncoder.js, dist/utils/processTracker.js and .d.ts, and dist/services/browserManager.js never SIGKILL FFmpeg or the browser; one SIGTERM, then a stall report. dist/utils/gpuEncoder.js and .d.ts and dist/index.js and .d.ts export gpuProbesExited, so a GPU encoder probe past its deadline stays counted until it exits. dist/utils/gpuEncoder.js gives the trial encode of a GPU encoder 30 s, not 2 s, before it counts that encoder as unusable: a deadline for a hung session, not a busy machine; and it takes the GPU encoder family the host names (HYPERFRAMES_GPU_ENCODER) without detecting one. dist/utils/processTracker.js and .d.ts, dist/services/browserManager.js, dist/services/hdrCapture.js and dist/index.js and .d.ts tell a listener (onChildProcess) the pid of every FFmpeg, ffprobe and Chrome process as it starts (Chrome at its spawn, through @puppeteer/browsers onBrowserSpawn, before its launch waits for DevTools), so the caller records it in its hardware session slot. dist/services/browserManager.js and .d.ts and dist/index.js and .d.ts keep the Chrome sandbox on when the host asks (HYPERFRAMES_CHROME_SANDBOX, chromeSandboxArgs), keep the WebGL vendor and renderer the GPU probe saw, for the host to log (browserGpuProbe), and on Linux run hardware mode on ANGLE over Vulkan instead of EGL. dist/services/drawElementService.js and dist/services/frameCapture.js capture a drawElement frame only from its own canvas paint event: upstream drew the last recorded snapshot after 250 ms without one; patched, the capture waits, and a paint that has not come in 10 s fails the drawElement attempt recoverably (HF_DE_PAINT_TIMEOUT), which the producer re-renders by screenshot. dist/services/drawElementService.js feature-detects Chrome 155+ canvas content=drawable and marks only the composition root drawable; modern draws preserve source element geometry, while the legacy layoutsubtree path is retained.
